data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/tmp/dispatch-dev-1.md\", \"content\": \"This is your first work dispatch. Implement exactly this in the subject\\nrepository, on your own branch:\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` containing a function `greet(name)` that returns the string\\n   `\\\"Hello, \u003cname\u003e!\\\"` (i.e. `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`), where `\u003cname\u003e` is replaced by\\n   the `name` argument passed in.\\n\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` containing unit tests (use the `unittest` module)\\n   that cover at least:\\n   - a normal name, e.g. `greet(\\\"World\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, World!\\\"`\\n   - the empty string, e.g. `greet(\\\"\\\")` returns `\\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n\\n3. Verify your work yourself before committing by running, from the repo\\n   root:\\n\\n       python3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n\\n   It must exit 0 (all tests passing). Fix anything that doesn't.\\n\\n4. Commit both files to your own branch\\n   (cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>). Do not touch any other branch\\n   or file outside `src/` and `tests/`.\\n\\n5. Reply honestly: state clearly whether you ran the test command yourself\\n   and what its result was, and confirm both files are committed. If anything\\n   didn't work, say so plainly rather than reporting success.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":0,"type":"content_block_delta"}

